    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s June 10th slate, the centerpiece of our lineup is undoubtedly **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands an elite score of 76.67. Despite facing a lefty in Rod\u00f3n, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains our most bankable asset, buoyed by an favorable order position and a steady base projection that holds up against mid-tier SP skill. Supporting him at the top of the range is **Bryson Stott** (72.46), who leverages a significant platoon edge against Scherzer to provide high-ceiling potential. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** (66.94) enters as a strong start; his positive dynamic platoon adjustment against Sproat makes him a high-efficiency play today, despite facing a middle-of-the-pack SP_xERA.\n\nThe decision-making process for the remaining slots favored players with clear platoon advantages or favorable park factors. We are rolling with **Gleyber Torres** (59.17) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.38) despite middling SP matchups, as their order slots and moderate platoon benefits squeeze enough value out of the ATC projections to keep them comfortably in the starting rotation. **Taylor Ward** also earns a nod at 55.54, with a +16% park factor compensation helping to mitigate the risk of facing the talented Kirby. Conversely, the \"tough decision\" of the day involved **Geraldo Perdomo** (44.86); he was the most viable bench candidate, but his score was ultimately capped by a negative SP skill adjustment and park factors that made him less efficient than the starters ahead of him. \n\nRegarding risks, we are carefully monitoring the situation around **Masyn Winn**, who sits on the bench with a 44.02 score. His utility is currently depressed by a 34% rain risk, and while he possesses an elite catching frame, he remains an emergency option only. We continue to hold **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith** on the bench due to status issues, and we will avoid deploying them to protect our daily game caps. For the remainder of our roster\u2014including **Jonathan Aranda**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014we are prepared to rotate them in as daily lineup conditions evolve.",
